    "body": "Hello,\r\nIn the terminal, if i type jupyter notebook, it will connect to a server and opens an untitled.ipynb and if i want to close the kernel, then in the terminal if  i type cntrl+c and then y, the kernel closes. Next time if i want to open a new notebook, then it will be automatically named as Untitled1.ipynb.\r\nSo,\r\n1) How can i assign a specific name for the notebook i want to run (such that if i name each .ipynb files differently, it is easy for identification...)\r\n2) For running jupyter notebook, it should connect every time to the server only..?? Is there no possibility to just open within the system (if opened in the server there is a chance of data breaching..??) or sometimes if there is no internet, then it is not possible to run the jupyter notebook right.?\r\n\r\nHow do i solve these issues..??\r\n\r\nAny suggestions are appreciated.\r\n\r\nThank you.",
